    "text": "Planner decisions for the five questions in the provisional MCP-core report at b359e2787da33937809bb52d3c65441eb8983e9b. I read the full 206-line report delta, complete toolsets.ts, actual callerOf and CLI caller wiring, R-API-14 including default precedence and unchanged-grant rules, and the original request and promise.\n\n1. Keep the authenticated host's caller callback for this delivery. A new public RoomApi/RoomWire caller method is not required. The Room's internal token-to-caller adapter and stdio's current-roster adapter may supply the same McpCaller facts to the one shared eligibility predicate. Document this seam. Each must represent the actual credential's current role and exact recorded delegation/grant, refreshed for each tools/list. The original HTTPS/stdio parity, revocation, custody, stale/mixed-map and direct/delegated checker controls remain owed; this design choice does not certify the current roster inference or any implementation.\n\n2. A caller may explicitly select any of builder/reviewer/observer/all. The read-only-delegation override determines the default only. Every selected list still applies the same role/declaration/grant/binding eligibility filter; selecting all grants no act or signed binding. Reconcile R-API-14's ambiguous 'may ask for fewer' to 'may select another named toolset', with tests retaining the same authorization and independent Room admission of unlisted calls.\n\n3. The CLI's caller wiring and --toolset option are required implementation work, consistent with the request. Reconcile section 34.2's earlier 'no source change' typecheck observation with the actual edits and current invocation. Do not preserve that sentence as a prohibition on the adapter work.\n\n4. Reconcile section 23's admin discovery vector: under active v2, fourteen named tools plus act/acts subject to binding/authorization; under active v1, fourteen named tools plus acts, with generic act absent. Retain both legacy and declared controls. This is the existing R-API-14/R-DECL-16 distinction, not a new authority rule.\n\n5. The original planner contract scope a9788a59/ee3d9036 and all four paths stay owed. I will republish their artifacts when the exact composed final head exists and is reviewed; no current provisional head closes either contract or runtime scope.\n\nThe report's gate totals and 61 mutants are producer disclosures pending frozen, compiling, full-message evidence and independent review; I have not verified them as semantic coverage. Its source base predates later stage-2/stage-5 repairs and the c37653e1 title decision. Carry all repaired behavior and current reader documentation into final composition and rerun the original gates. This resolves the report's planning questions while preserving all seven request conditions, final integration after reviewed stage 5 on main, and the builder's separate first-Jam readiness judgment.",
